---
// The speed plan as a picture: the ceiling the limits set, and the plan that fits under it
// by speeding up as hard as allowed and braking just in time.
---

<figure class="diagram not-content">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 310" role="img" aria-label="Speed against distance along a path. The plan rises from rest, drops for a turn, rises again and brakes to a stop at the end.">
    <!-- axes -->
    <line class="d-rule" x1="60" y1="250" x2="690" y2="250"></line>
    <line class="d-rule" x1="60" y1="250" x2="60" y2="30"></line>
    <line class="d-soft" x1="60" y1="60" x2="690" y2="60"></line>
    <text x="14" y="36">SPEED</text>
    <text x="16" y="64">TOP</text>
    <text x="38" y="254">0</text>
    <text x="370" y="296" text-anchor="middle">DISTANCE ALONG THE PATH, s</text>
    <text x="60" y="270">START</text>
    <text x="664" y="270">END</text>

    <!-- the ceiling: the fastest the robot may go at each point -->
    <path class="d-ink d-dash" d="M60 60 L270 60 C320 60 330 170 370 170 C410 170 420 60 470 60 L680 60"></path>

    <!-- the plan -->
    <path class="d-accent" d="M60 250 C90 150 150 80 220 60 L250 60 C310 78 345 125 370 170 C395 125 430 78 490 60 L520 60 C590 80 650 150 680 250"></path>

    <circle class="f-accent" cx="60" cy="250" r="4"></circle>
    <circle class="f-accent" cx="680" cy="250" r="4"></circle>

    <text x="118" y="200" class="t-accent">SPEED UP</text>
    <text x="118" y="214">FORWARD PASS</text>
    <text x="286" y="132" class="t-accent" text-anchor="end">BRAKE</text>
    <text x="370" y="226" text-anchor="middle">THE TURN'S LIMIT</text>
    <line class="d-ink" x1="370" y1="178" x2="370" y2="212"></line>
    <text x="622" y="200" class="t-accent" text-anchor="end">BRAKE IN TIME</text>
    <text x="622" y="214" text-anchor="end">BACKWARD PASS</text>
    <text x="300" y="50" text-anchor="middle">CEILING</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The dashed line is the fastest the robot may go at each point. The plan is the fastest curve that stays under
    it, can be reached from the start, and can still stop at the end.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
